def longest_run(text):
    if not text:
        return 0

    max_run = 1
    current_run = 1

    for i in range(1, len(text)):
        if text[i] == text[i - 1]:
            current_run += 1
            max_run = max(max_run, current_run)
        else:
            current_run = 1

    return max_run
```

This function works by iterating through the input string `text` and keeping track of the length of the current run of consecutive characters. It updates the maximum run length found so far (`max_run`) whenever it sees a longer run. When it encounters a different character, it resets the current run length to 1. The function returns the maximum run length found, or 0 for an empty string.

